# Capstone Project Stack & Conventions

## Tech Stack
- Runtime: Node.js (LTS)
- Language: JavaScript
- Package Manager: npm

## Code Conventions
- Use camelCase for variables and functions
- Use PascalCase for classes
- Write descriptive commit messages following Conventional Commits
- Keep functions small and focused
- Source files must be UTF-8 (never UTF-16). `node src/index.js` must parse without a BOM/encoding SyntaxError.

## Project Structure
- `/src` — application source code
- `/tests` — test files
- `/docs` — documentation

## Settings feature (testable)
- Persist settings only after `src/settingsSchema.js` Joi validation succeeds. Never write `config.json` on invalid input.
- Allowed fields are only `name` (trimmed, 2-80 chars), `email` (Joi email, stored lowercase), `theme` (`light` | `dark` | `system`), and `notifications` (boolean). Unknown keys must be rejected, not saved.
- `index.js` must not seed or overwrite user settings with hardcoded demo data on startup. First run opens the form; later runs print saved settings.

## Verification
- Changes to `settingsSchema.js` or `settingsManager.js` must include tests under `/tests` that write to a temp file (not the real `config.json`) and pass via `npm test`.

## AI Assistant Rules
- Always ask before generating large files
- Prefer modern ES6+ syntax
- Explain complex logic with inline comments
- Do not accept a settings-form change as done until `npm test` has been run in the session
